# Parcel check builds

When verifying that the app still bundles (compile check), **do not** run plain `parcel build` into `dist/` or use the default `.parcel-cache` — that races `parcel serve` HMR and overwrites Electron/Cap static `dist/`.

Use:

```bash
pnpm run build:check
```

(`--dist-dir .tmp/parcel-check` + `--cache-dir .tmp/parcel-check-cache`)

Only write to `dist/` when the user explicitly asks for a real build/deploy (`build`, `build:electron`, `build:cap`, etc.).
